many people working in the healthcare  sector chose their profession because  they were interested in health  obviously health is unbelievably  important but an enormous driver of  what's happening in the sector now is  economics  in order to understand fully the forces  that are shaping the evolution of the  health care sector you need to  understand the underlying economic  drivers that affect patients providers  and payers  all leaders whether they be on the  purchasing side or on the provider side  or even working with patients need to  understand those forces so they can  anticipate the challenges that they will  face and structure their activities to  meet those challenges  you'll explore healthcare spending  growth  consider how new technologies and  services lead to higher spending  and examine how changes to benefit  design and payment reform can promote a  fiscally sustainable health system that  delivers high quality care we need to  decide what kind of care should be  provided and not just leave it up to a  system that's broken that helps escalate  these costs primary care is the long  game it's not about sort of dumping  everything out in one 20-minute visit  we'll use conversations with industry  experts real-world examples and  interactive lessons to help you create  more effective growth strategies better  negotiate reimbursements and  partnerships and become an advocate for  healthcare economics both inside and  outside of your organization come  explore the economic forces shaping  healthcare  [Music]
 

